title: 'Migrate `claims` to `#[pallet::authorize]`, keeping bare claims during the transition'

doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    The `claim` and `claim_attest` calls of `polkadot_runtime_common::claims` carry
    `#[pallet::authorize]` and accept a general transaction, in addition to the bare (unsigned)
    transaction they accepted before. The deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` impl stays until claim
    tooling can submit general transactions (polkadot-js/api#6276, polkadot-js/apps#12446,
    polkadot-api/polkadot-api#760). A follow-up removes it before the SDK removes
    `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` after April 2027.

    The validation semantics do not change. A bare and a general transaction run the same checks
    and produce the same transaction validity. The two calls accept a `None` or an `Authorized`
    origin.

    `weight_of_authorize` is zero, because the `claim` and `claim_attest` weights already include
    their validation. The `WeightInfo` trait is unchanged.

    To accept general `claim` transactions, a runtime must include `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in
    its transaction extension pipeline. No change is needed to keep bare claims working.

crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-common
  bump: minor
